              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "The latest models in the iPhone lineup are the **iPhone 17 series** (including the iPhone 17, the ultra-thin iPhone 17 Air, the iPhone 17 Pro, and the iPhone 17 Pro Max). \n\nYou can purchase the latest iPhone through several official and authorized channels, depending on your location and how you prefer to pay:\n\n### 1. Directly from Apple (Best for Trade-Ins & Financing)\nBuying directly from Apple ensures you get an unlocked device with the most seamless buying experience.\n* **Apple Store Online:** You can order directly via [apple.com](https://www.apple.com) or through the **Apple Store app** on iOS. Apple offers free delivery or the option for in-store pickup at your nearest location.\n* **Apple Retail Stores:** If you have an Apple Store nearby, you can buy one in person, test out the different models (like comparing the standard iPhone 17 to the ultra-thin iPhone 17 Air), and have a specialist help you set it up.\n* **Benefits:** Access to **Apple Trade In** (which gives you immediate credit toward your purchase when trading in an older device) and **0% financing options** (like the iPhone Upgrade Program or Apple Card Monthly Installments).\n\n### 2. Major Mobile Carriers (Best for Contract Deals & Subsidized Prices)\nIf you are willing to lock into a multi-year service contract or upgrade your current cellular plan, network carriers often offer the most aggressive discounts (sometimes making the phone \"free\" via bill credits with a qualifying trade-in).\n* **In the US:** Verizon, AT&T, and T-Mobile.\n* **In the UK/Europe:** EE, Vodafone, O2, Three, and Orange. \n* **Benefits:** Highly subsidized pricing, convenient monthly billing integrated with your cellular service, and flexible upgrade plans.\n\n### 3. Authorized Retailers & E-commerce Platforms (Best for Rewards & General Deals)\nMajor third-party retail stores and online marketplaces carry the latest iPhones and frequently offer their own store-specific financing, loyalty points, or bundle deals.\n* **In North America:** Best Buy, Target, Walmart, Costco, and Amazon.\n* **In Europe & International:** MediaMarkt (various European countries), Currys (UK), eMAG, iSTYLE, or Altex (Eastern Europe). \n* **Benefits:** Store credit card rewards, regional availability in areas without a physical Apple Store, and occasional sales/discounts on accessories.\n\n*Note: Since the annual iPhone cycle typically refreshes in September, the next-generation **iPhone 18 series** is expected to be announced in September 2026. If you can wait a few months, you will either be able to buy the brand-new model or purchase the iPhone 17 series at a discounted price.*",
